    <worksheet name='CR Level 2'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontsize='12'>Top N &lt;Sheet Name&gt;</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>Top N created using this tutorial : </run>
            <run auto-url='true' hyperlink='tabdoc:load-url url=&amp;quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z0R9OsDl-10&amp;amp;ab_channel=Tableau&amp;quot;'>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z0R9OsDl-10&amp;ab_channel=Tableau</run>
            <run>

But there are a few caveats --
1.  it cannot break ties. i.e if you want to display top 5 and there are 10 items with the same top value , Tableau selects randomly 3 to display
2. it cannot order the stacked bars based onTop N  % Served Chats. reasons unknown

For a true list that overcomes these caveats please refer to &quot;RR CR Level 2 (no ties)&quot; viz</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
